# Build-context ignore list for Dockerfile.development only. BuildKit reads
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore instead of .dockerignore when it exists, so this
# file replaces .dockerignore for the dev image and leaves the production
# image's list alone.
#
# It matches .dockerignore except for one line: .devcontainer stays in the
# context, because Dockerfile.development COPYs .devcontainer/setup.sh and
# .devcontainer/config-files/. Keep the two files in step otherwise.

.db
node_modules
npm-debug.log
.venv
.git
.github
.claude
.mailpit-data
ai-plans
ai-tools
docs
infrastructure
junit
staticfiles
mediafiles
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.env
.env.docker

# Test support. The production image installs no dev dependencies (`uv sync
# --no-dev`), and di_core's `container.wire(packages=INTERNAL_INSTALLED_APPS)`
# imports EVERY module under those packages at startup -- so one shipped test
# module importing model_bakery crashes web, worker, beat and release alike:
#
#   File "/home/user/app/common/tests/test_org_retrievers.py", line 21
#     from model_bakery import baker
#   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'model_bakery'
#
# `factories.py` is test support too, despite living at app level, and every
# one of them imports model_bakery. The development image gets all of this back
# through the compose bind mount (`./:/home/user/app/`), and CI runs pytest via
# `uv run`, not in this image.
**/tests
**/testing
**/factories.py
**/fixtures.py
conftest.py
